  "body": "## What changed\n\nMost mill generators seed their path at X0 Y0 on the clearance plane. That point is the world origin. The opening rapid started there, so these items read the world origin and not G54:\n- the viewport (the drawn approach);\n- the simulation link between operations;\n- the CL `START` line;\n- the post engine's `StartX/Y/Z`.\n\nThe posted move blocks were already correct, because a post writes only the end of each move.\n\nThe fix:\n- New `Toolpath::seat_approach` (`crates/cl/src/cl/path_approach.rs`). When the first move is a rapid that leaves the seed, the start of that rapid moves to the WCS origin (X/Y) on the same plane. The end of the rapid does not change.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` calls it after generation. The call comes before the yaw exit, the fixture routing and the verify laws, so those laws judge the new rapid. The origin comes from `wcs_context`, which is the same origin that the post subtracts. A 3+2 path reads the origin in its local frame (`TiltedFrame::to_local`).\n- These paths do not change: paths that open at their own first point (holes, plasma, sinker, lathe, wire, rotary, 3D roughing, adaptive trochoidal), and a zero-length seed rapid.\n\nThe cause has existed since 942a36d65 (#690 / #697, v0.17). It is not a 0.23 regression. The reproduction and the family list are on #2382.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2382-wcs-start.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Reporter's project (local copy, not attached): each operation opened with a rapid from X0 Y0 at the clearance height. G54 is at a stock corner far from that point. The project does not post, because of a correct refusal that is not related to this issue (Home after Pause).\n- Fixture (G54 at X40 Y20 Z10.5): on main, the face and the parallel finish start at (0, 0, 30). With the fix, they start at (40, 20, 30).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/wcs_start.rs`:\n  - `a_2d_operation_starts_over_the_wcs_origin` (fails on main)\n  - `a_3d_operation_starts_over_the_wcs_origin` (fails on main)\n  - `a_hole_operation_starts_over_its_first_hole`\n  - `the_posted_program_measures_from_g54_and_never_visits_the_world_origin`\n- `crates/cl/tests/origin_approach.rs`:\n  - `seat_approach_moves_the_seeded_start_to_the_wcs_origin`\n  - `seat_approach_leaves_other_openings_alone`\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`. A change in `cl` makes the quick gate fall back to batch. I ran the steps of the crates downstream of `cl` (`--only debug cl post sim motion app ui clippy`): 804 steps, 0 failed, about 116 min. I did not run the geometry, kernel and tools steps, because those crates do not depend on `cl`.\n- No golden and no count changed. `golden_cl`, `first_router_part`, `axis_direction` and `wcs_rotation_control` pass without edits.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI was not started. The viewport reading comes from the toolpath data that the viewport draws.\n- A 3+2 path with a moved WCS has no own pinning test. The code reads the origin through `to_local`, and the existing tilt suites pass.\n- 5-axis contour and parallel (stamped finishing paths) have no own pinning test with a moved WCS.\n- A separate display question is still open: the chain pick ring and the toolpath in an aligned setup. This PR does not change it.\n\nChangelog: The opening approach of each milling operation now starts over the setup's WCS origin, not the world origin. This applies to the viewport, the simulation and the program start point.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2382\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
